              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Slope decides it more than lawn size. On flat ground under about a quarter acre, a push mower is lighter, cheaper, easier to pivot around obstacles, and has one fewer system to fail. On any real slope, or for anyone with back, knee, or shoulder limitations, self-propulsion is worth the cost and weight.
              </p>
