              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">What size lawn can a push mower handle?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                A push mower is comfortable up to about a quarter acre on flat ground, and workable up to half an acre for anyone who does not mind the walk. Above half an acre, or on any lawn with real slope, self-propulsion stops being a luxury. Above an acre, a riding mower is the right tool regardless.
