              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">How high should I cut my grass?</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm leading-relaxed">
                Most cool-season lawns do best at three to four inches, which is higher than most people cut. Taller grass shades the soil, holds moisture, develops deeper roots, and crowds out weeds, and cutting less material per pass makes a push mower noticeably easier to push. Never remove more than a third of the blade height in one cut.
